# An X session on Dolly's display: the Xsdl server, twm managing the
# windows, and three of X's own clients in theirs: a clock, eyes that follow
# the pointer and a terminal with a shell, where imgui-x11 starts Dear ImGui's
# example in a window of its own.
FROM /v0.1.4/Dollyfile-system f1fa8104555572ab95996ed6b89ad705419e6cb5729d4b291a9da0276cee4ee7
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/x11/Dollyfile-xorg-server 35e9b5937dc8f4f6f307dd45bbfe26ab742a4b7a15cc51ba6d067aa8e45df53c
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/x11/Dollyfile-twm e5aad06129ab0d45e1220613903fbebbc8a497739f84073ac54225a2423c5b15
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/x11/Dollyfile-xclock 5ed3ec59efc6ac7e425009494d12bc5f0c2b5a052889b3cf80f73885335bd461
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/x11/Dollyfile-xeyes c36df43cd2beb87b0b74f07cd9c60803d76cc8284057d83f2169bd71f3d6a7d5
INSTALL /v0.1.4/demos/x11/Dollyfile-xterm 0c8651fd2d049732f3facc85949fd0b8a2ce6dec675fe6bc72560d17b94708a9
# amy installs packages into the session (tmux, nvim and the rest), with the
